    "body": "**Live-GUI check, driven over MCP** (M5 session, macOS, the `camcraft-ui-428` build of this branch, launched with `--mcp-port 7333`):\n- The GUI logged `mcp: listening on 127.0.0.1:7333`, and `camcraft-cli mcp --connect 127.0.0.1:7333` served the full tool table (40 tools).\n- `open_project` is **refused** in a live session (\"would replace the user's document without the app's unsaved-changes prompt\"), so an agent cannot swap the user's document.\n- `add_tool` (EM-0600-4FL) and `set_stock` (40×40×10) landed in the running app's document.\n- `add_operation` (\"Agent face\") appeared in `get_job`, read back from the live app.\n- `undo` removed it and `redo` brought it back, using the app's own history (`can_undo` / `can_redo` track the GUI's stack).\n- The window closed cleanly afterwards.\n\n**Not exercised by hand:** pressing Cmd+Z in the window itself and watching the browser tree update. The MCP undo goes through the same History the shortcut uses. Fork synced at v0.15.0.",
