    "body": "Back to draft for a security fix from the review (M3 session). A web page in the user's browser can `POST` to the live MCP port with a `text/plain` body. The HTTP header lines fail as -32700, but the body line still runs as JSON-RPC, so a page could call `save_project`, `post`, `import_model` or `export_tool_library` with its own paths. Fixing before merge:\n- refuse and drop any connection whose first line is not a JSON-RPC object (e.g. an HTTP request line);\n- bound the line read before it grows past the cap;\n- add a write timeout so a stalled client cannot block the listener.",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
