    "updated_at": "2026-11-09T22:32:56Z",
    "body": "Security fix pushed (`c051ba9d`), from the review's browser drive-by finding:\n- **JSON-RPC lines only.** Every non-blank wire line must open a JSON object or array. An HTTP request line or header gets a `-32600` refusal and the connection closes before any line reaches the app, so a web page can no longer smuggle a JSON-RPC body (`save_project`, `post`, `export_tool_library`) past its own HTTP headers.\n- **Bounded read:** at most the 16 MiB cap is buffered, checked as it reads.\n- **Write timeout:** 5 s, so a stalled client cannot hold the listener.\n\nPinned by `mcp_live::a_browser_post_never_reaches_the_app`: a raw `POST / HTTP/1.1` with a `save_project` body is refused and closed, nothing reaches the inbox, and a real JSON client is still served on the next connection. With the rule disabled, that test fails in 3 s (\"the page's request reached the app\").\n\n`mcp_live` 7/7 and clippy are clean. A per-session token was considered and dropped (see the decision record). Flagging ready again for a re-review of the fix.",
